WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.436 --> 00:00:02.457
Good evening.

2
00:00:02.477 --> 00:00:03.577
[s@Good evening.

3
00:00:03.597 --> 00:00:03.918
Who are you?

4
00:00:04.078 --> 00:00:04.838
I'm a red fox.

5
00:00:05.378 --> 00:00:07.299
Red foxes are mammals.

6
00:00:09.501 --> 00:00:11.882
We look like dogs.

7
00:00:31.892 --> 00:00:32.953
Where do you live?

8
00:00:34.734 --> 00:00:37.756
Red foxes live all over the world.

9
00:00:40.218 --> 00:00:41.499
We like forests.

10
00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:46.882
But we also live in cities and deserts.

11
00:00:49.964 --> 00:00:51.886
You eat mice, right?

12
00:00:53.407 --> 00:00:57.149
Yes. We eat other small animals too.

13
00:00:58.830 --> 00:01:01.072
We like birds and rabbits.

14
00:01:03.584 --> 00:01:07.086
Sometimes we eat fruit—and garbage.

15
00:01:09.487 --> 00:01:11.288
Your ears are big!

16
00:01:12.809 --> 00:01:14.990
Red foxes are good hunters.

17
00:01:16.831 --> 00:01:19.513
Our big ears help us hear prey.

18
00:01:21.634 --> 00:01:23.015
Who are your enemies?

19
00:01:25.196 --> 00:01:27.817
Coyotes and bears hunt us.

20
00:01:29.178 --> 00:01:31.319
People are our enemies too.

21
00:01:33.248 --> 00:01:35.849
They hunt us and build near our dens.

22
00:01:37.770 --> 00:01:40.071
Oh! Is that your den?

23
00:01:41.311 --> 00:01:44.113
Yes. We use dens for sleeping.

24
00:01:46.073 --> 00:01:49.175
Mother foxes keep their babies in dens.

25
00:01:51.376 --> 00:01:53.076
I like your bushy tail!

26
00:01:54.677 --> 00:01:57.398
We use our tails to cover our bodies.

27
00:01:58.779 --> 00:02:01.080
This keeps us warm at nap time.

28
00:02:07.886 --> 00:02:09.870
Shh. I hear a mouse.

29
00:02:11.493 --> 00:02:12.675
I'm going to hunt!

30
00:02:15.420 --> 00:02:17.023
So long, Red Fox!
